The work item:

{
  "key": "AP-19",
  "title": "Run ApolloStorage as a Pekko cluster",
  "body": "ApolloStorage runs as a single node: the projection is one instance and bucket entities are hosted by a node-local BucketEntityManager. That is a throughput and availability ceiling \u2014 one process is the whole system. To scale horizontally and survive a node failure the service must run as a Pekko cluster.\n\nForm a cluster across replicas with automatic membership and a split-brain resolver (keep-majority). Replace the single-node BucketEntityManager with Cluster Sharding, so each bucket is a cluster-wide singleton entity addressed by EntityRef; persistence ids and the journal are unchanged. Distribute the projection with ShardedDaemonProcess across N slice ranges, rebalanced on membership change. Cluster formation via Pekko Management and discovery, with a management HTTP port for bootstrap and health.",
  "type_hint": null,
  "status": "open",
  "url": "https://example.invalid/AP-19",
  "source": "github-issues",
  "labels": [],
  "links": []
}

Its triage artifact:

