prompt.raw:
You are executing the following Claude Code skill.

<skill>
Challenge this breakdown: try to find the holes in it and give a verdict.

Return JSON with: item, target, verdict, attacks, findings. verdict is REFUTED, WEAKENED or SURVIVED. Each attack has attack, method, result. Each finding has finding, evidence.
</skill>

The work item:

{
  "key": "HP-12",
  "title": "Expose a Prometheus /metrics endpoint",
  "body": "The observability stack scrapes each service's Prometheus /metrics endpoint; Apollo and Hermes already expose one. Hephaestus has none, so it is invisible to Prometheus and Grafana \u2014 no JVM health, no worker throughput, no failure rate.\n\nAdd GET /metrics on the existing HTTP port alongside /health, rendering the app CollectorRegistry. Use the same Prometheus simpleclient the sibling services use. A metrics.enabled toggle defaults to true; when disabled there is no route and a no-op recorder. Base JVM metrics plus worker metrics through a MetricsRecorder seam injected into the JobConsumer: jobs processed by lane and outcome, a processing-time histogram, and an in-flight gauge.",
  "type_hint": null,
  "status": "open",
  "url": "https://example.invalid/HP-12",
  "source": "github-issues",
  "labels": [],
  "links": []
}

Its triage artifact:

{
  "item": "HP-12",
  "type": "feature",
  "path": "standard",
  "domains": [
    "backend"
  ],
  "summary": "Expose a Prometheus /metrics endpoint",
  "rationale": "new observable surface inside one service, following an established pattern. Corrected 2026-10-20: was [backend, infra]; the item changes a route, a registry and a config toggle inside the service \u2014 the scrape side is not in scope here",
  "handoff": false,
  "handoff_reason": null,
  "architecture_change": false,
  "breaking_change": false
}

The breakdown under challenge:

{
  "item": "HP-12",
  "epics": [
    {
      "id": "E1",
      "title": "Operator can scrape Hephaestus's /metrics endpoint",
      "stories": [
        {
          "id": "S1",
          "statement": "Expose GET /metrics on the existing HTTP port, rendering the app CollectorRegistry via the Prometheus simpleclient the sibling services use",
          "domains": [
            "backend"
          ],
          "acceptance_criteria": [
            {
              "id": "AC1",
              "given": "metrics.enabled is true (the default) and the service is running",
              "when": "a client sends GET /metrics on the existing HTTP port",
              "then": "the response is 200 with a Prometheus text-format body rendered from the app CollectorRegistry"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "S2",
          "statement": "A metrics.enabled toggle, defaulting to true, controls whether the /metrics route exists and whether a real or no-op recorder is used",
          "domains": [
            "backend"
          ],
          "acceptance_criteria": [
            {
              "id": "AC1",
              "given": "metrics.enabled is not set in configuration",
              "when": "the service starts",
              "then": "metrics.enabled resolves to true and the /metrics route is registered"
            },
            {
              "id": "AC2",
              "given": "metrics.enabled is set to false",
              "when": "a client sends GET /metrics",
              "then": "no /metrics route exists and the request is not handled by a metrics handler"
            },
            {
              "id": "AC3",
              "given": "metrics.enabled is set to false",
              "when": "the JobConsumer processes a job",
              "then": "a no-op MetricsRecorder is used and no metric is recorded"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "S3",
          "statement": "The exposed registry includes base JVM metrics alongside worker metrics",
          "domains": [
            "backend"
          ],
          "acceptance_criteria": [
            {
              "id": "AC1",
              "given": "metrics.enabled is true",
              "when": "a client sends GET /metrics",
              "then": "the response body includes base JVM metrics (e.g. memory and GC) from the CollectorRegistry"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "E2",
      "title": "Operator can observe worker throughput and health through MetricsRecorder-backed metrics",
      "stories": [
        {
          "id": "S4",
          "statement": "The MetricsRecorder seam injected into the JobConsumer records jobs processed by lane and outcome",
          "domains": [
            "backend"
          ],
          "acceptance_criteria": [
            {
              "id": "AC1",
              "given": "the JobConsumer processes a job in a given lane and the job completes successfully",
              "when": "processing finishes",
              "then": "MetricsRecorder increments a jobs-processed counter labeled with that lane and outcome=success"
            },
            {
              "id": "AC2",
              "given": "the JobConsumer processes a job in a given lane and the job fails",
              "when": "processing finishes",
              "then": "MetricsRecorder increments a jobs-processed counter labeled with that lane and outcome=failure"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "S5",
          "statement": "The MetricsRecorder seam records job processing time in a histogram",
          "domains": [
            "backend"
          ],
          "acceptance_criteria": [
            {
              "id": "AC1",
              "given": "the JobConsumer processes a job",
              "when": "processing finishes",
              "then": "MetricsRecorder records the elapsed processing time as an observation in a processing-time histogram"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "S6",
          "statement": "The MetricsRecorder seam tracks the number of jobs currently in flight via a gauge",
          "domains": [
            "backend"
          ],
          "acceptance_criteria": [
            {
              "id": "AC1",
              "given": "the JobConsumer begins processing a job",
              "when": "processing starts",
              "then": "MetricsRecorder increments the in-flight gauge"
            },
            {
              "id": "AC2",
              "given": "the JobConsumer has started processing a job",
              "when": "processing finishes, whether it succeeds or fails",
              "then": "MetricsRecorder decrements the in-flight gauge"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "E3",
      "title": "Grafana dashboards and alerting for worker throughput",
      "stories": [
        {
          "id": "S7",
          "statement": "Build a Grafana dashboard showing jobs processed by lane and outcome, processing time and in-flight work.",
          "domains": [
            "infra"
          ],
          "acceptance_criteria": [
            {
              "id": "AC1",
              "given": "the service is being scraped",
              "when": "an operator opens the worker dashboard",
              "then": "jobs processed by lane and outcome are plotted over the selected window"
            },
            {
              "id": "AC2",
              "given": "the worker dashboard is open",
              "when": "processing time is inspected",
              "then": "the histogram's quantiles are rendered per lane"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "S8",
          "statement": "Add alerting rules that page when the failure rate or in-flight work crosses its threshold.",
          "domains": [
            "infra"
          ],
          "acceptance_criteria": [
            {
              "id": "AC1",
              "given": "the failure rate is above its configured threshold",
              "when": "the alerting rules evaluate",
              "then": "an alert fires with the lane in its labels"
            },
            {
              "id": "AC2",
              "given": "in-flight work is within its threshold",
              "when": "the alerting rules evaluate",
              "then": "no alert fires"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}

