{
  "key": "HP-12",
  "title": "Expose a Prometheus /metrics endpoint",
  "body": "The observability stack scrapes each service's Prometheus /metrics endpoint; Apollo and Hermes already expose one. Hephaestus has none, so it is invisible to Prometheus and Grafana \u2014 no JVM health, no worker throughput, no failure rate.\n\nAdd GET /metrics on the existing HTTP port alongside /health, rendering the app CollectorRegistry. Use the same Prometheus simpleclient the sibling services use. A metrics.enabled toggle defaults to true; when disabled there is no route and a no-op recorder. Base JVM metrics plus worker metrics through a MetricsRecorder seam injected into the JobConsumer: jobs processed by lane and outcome, a processing-time histogram, and an in-flight gauge.",
  "type_hint": null,
